--- BUF-01, BUF-05: declaration forms and exact capacity ---
Create a buffer called cupboard.
If cupboard's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {cupboard's size}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's size.
a buffer called 'toolbox' is 1 bytes.
If 'toolbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's size.
If 'toolbox's capacity is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 1 got {'toolbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's capacity.
a buffer called ledger is 83196 bytes.
If ledger's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {ledger's size}", Exit 95. Print ledger's size.
Print 0 times 0.
If ledger's capacity is not 83196 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 83196 got {ledger's capacity}", Exit 95. Print ledger's capacity.
Print ledger's size.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  Create a buffer called cupboard,
  If cupboard's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {cupboard's size}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's size,
  a buffer called 'toolbox' is 1 bytes,
  If 'toolbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's size,
  If 'toolbox's capacity is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 1 got {'toolbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's capacity,
  a buffer called ledger is 83196 bytes,
  If ledger's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {ledger's size}", Exit 95. Print ledger's size,
  Print 0 times 0,
  If ledger's capacity is not 83196 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 83196 got {ledger's capacity}", Exit 95. Print ledger's capacity,
  Print ledger's size.

--- BUF-10, BUF-11, BUF-12: size, length, capacity, empty ---
a buffer called 'the greeting' is 7 bytes in size.
If 'the greeting's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 1 got {'the greeting's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's empty.
append "gtazsxa" to 'the greeting'.
If 'the greeting's size is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'the greeting's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's size.
If 'the greeting's capacity is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'the greeting's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's capacity.
If 'the greeting's length is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected 7 got {'the greeting's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's length.
If 'the greeting's length is not 'the greeting's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the greeting's size} got {'the greeting's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's length.
If 'the greeting's empty then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 0 got {'the greeting's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's empty.
Print 'the greeting's length.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'the greeting' is 7 bytes in size,
  If 'the greeting's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 1 got {'the greeting's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's empty,
  append "gtazsxa" to 'the greeting',
  If 'the greeting's size is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'the greeting's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's size,
  If 'the greeting's capacity is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'the greeting's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's capacity,
  If 'the greeting's length is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected 7 got {'the greeting's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's length,
  If 'the greeting's length is not 'the greeting's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the greeting's size} got {'the greeting's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's length,
  If 'the greeting's empty then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 0 got {'the greeting's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the greeting's empty,
  Print 'the greeting's length.

--- BUF-13: full, filled to capacity exactly ---
a buffer called 'the tray' is 73 bytes in size.
If 'the tray's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the tray's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the tray's full.
append "0lyb0hafw9q3o12bw5evkdm341mf09qbc9mfw5qzohi3k5ez816vgdy3clifotirw9ebwl6j" to 'the tray'.
If 'the tray's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the tray's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the tray's full.
append "c" to 'the tray'.
If 'the tray's full is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 1 got {'the tray's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the tray's full.
If 'the tray's size is not 73 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 73 got {'the tray's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the tray's size.
Print 'the tray's size.

--- BUF-13 again, a different split and a dynamic buffer ---
a buffer called 'the drawer' is 23 bytes in size.
If 'the drawer's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the drawer's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer's full.
append "un412bgtuf8tij0tano9i" to 'the drawer'.
If 'the drawer's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the drawer's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer's full.
append "k" to 'the drawer'.
If 'the drawer's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the drawer's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer's full.
append "9" to 'the drawer'.
If 'the drawer's full is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 1 got {'the drawer's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer's full.
If 'the drawer's size is not 23 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 23 got {'the drawer's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer's size.
a buffer called 'the crate'.
append "7s1efkpu7k5izw1yngd2v85" to 'the crate'.
Print 'the crate's full.
Print 'the drawer's size.

--- BUF-03: dynamic growth past the reserve ---
a buffer called 'the drawer'.
a number called 'the drawer appends made' is 0.
a boolean called 'the drawer overflowed' is false.
a boolean called 'the drawer found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the drawer found an error already pending' to true.
While 'the drawer appends made' is less than 269, append "vgp6fcdab41qfwtuv0leno9qr0x6fo" to 'the drawer', On error Set 'the drawer overflowed' to true. Set 'the drawer appends made' to 'the drawer appends made' add 1.
If 'the drawer's size is not 8070 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-03: expected 8070 got {'the drawer's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer's size.
If 'the drawer overflowed' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-03: expected 0 got {'the drawer overflowed'}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer overflowed'.
Print 'the drawer's size.

--- BUF-07: a read that truncates, detected by size ---
a text called 'pantry path' is "{'the workspace'}/buffer1".
open a file for writing called 'pantry being written' at 'pantry path'.
Write "oxibgx6b0xa7ktyzsp2fo1efsdm7wdyv0xmzclqb41y3glangtej4xmf4tqrgt6z4dyb0tirstujctynsdmfcd2j81uzshejw1u3cdunsdqfspqjo1" to 'pantry being written'.
Close 'pantry being written'.
open a file for reading called 'pantry being read' at 'pantry path'.
a buffer called pantry is 22 bytes in size.
a boolean called 'pantry was truncated' is false.
Read from 'pantry being read' into pantry.
On error Set 'pantry was truncated' to true.
Close 'pantry being read'.
If pantry's size is not 22 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-07: expected 22 got {pantry's size}", Exit 95. Print pantry's size.
If pantry's size is not pantry's capacity then, Print "ASSERT BUF-07: expected {pantry's capacity} got {pantry's size}", Exit 95. Print pantry's size.
Print pantry's size.

